---
title: "8 · The invoice list"
description: Find invoices with the amount cards, status tabs, search and filters; act on several invoices at once; export to CSV.
sidebar:
  order: 9
  label: "8 · The invoice list"
---

**Where:** **Invoices** in the left sidebar for the whole firm, or the **Invoices** tab of an opportunity, a company or a contact for one deal or one client.

## Amount cards

Four cards above the list sum up the invoices that match the current search and filters:

| Card | Amount shown |
|---|---|
| **Draft** | The total of the drafts. |
| **Awaiting payment** | What remains due on issued invoices, including overdue ones. |
| **Overdue** | What remains due on invoices past their due date. The card turns red when there is any. |
| **Paid this month** | The total of the invoices fully paid in the current calendar month (Singapore time). |

Select a card to show the matching tab; select it again to clear it. **Paid this month** opens the **Paid** tab with a **Paid this month** filter that can be removed. The cards are not shown for credit notes.

## Tabs and document type

The tabs **All**, **Draft**, **Awaiting payment**, **Overdue**, **Paid** and **Void** each show their count. **Awaiting payment** includes partially paid invoices.

Switch between **Invoices** and **Credit notes** to list one kind of document. On the credit note list, the **Awaiting payment** tab reads **Credit remaining**.

## Search and filters

- **Search number or client** finds an invoice by its number or by the client's name.
- The client selector (**All clients**) limits the list to one client.
- **Filters** opens the panel with **Issued between**, **Due between**, **Source** (invoices issued in Operon or uploaded), **Total between** and, when the firm has more than one issuing entity, **Issuing entity**.

Every active filter is shown as a chip above the table; select its cross to remove it, or select **Clear filters**. The **Filters** button shows how many filters are active. The cards, the tab counts and the totals all follow the search and the filters.

## Columns

| Column | Shows |
|---|---|
| **Number** | The invoice number, or **Draft**. Select it to open the invoice. |
| **Client** | The client, with the opportunity in grey under it. |
| **Source** | **Issued here** or **Uploaded**. |
| **Issued by** | The issuing entity. Shown only when the firm has more than one. |
| **Issued** / **Due** | The issue date and the due date. An overdue invoice shows its due date in red with, for example, **5 days overdue**. |
| **Total**, **Paid / credited**, **Amount due** | The amounts. On the credit note list, the last two read **Applied / refunded** and **Remaining**. |
| **Status** | The status. |
| **Sent / viewed** | Two marks: whether the invoice was emailed, and whether the client has viewed it. A mark that has not happened is dimmed. |

Select a column header to sort by it: once for ascending, again for descending, and a third time to return to the default order. Sorting covers all matching invoices, not only those on screen.

The last row of the table shows the number of matching invoices and the sums of **Total** and **Amount due** over all of them. When more invoices match than are shown, select **Load more**.

## Act on several invoices

Tick the invoices in the first column (or the box in the header to select all). A bar appears with:

| Action | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Issue selected** | Issues the selected drafts. |
| **Email selected** | Emails each selected issued invoice to its default recipient. |
| **Turn reminders off for selected** | Stops the payment reminders of the selected invoices. |
| **Export selected** | Downloads the selected rows as a CSV file. |
| **Clear selection** | Unticks every row and closes the bar. |

Each invoice is handled on its own. An invoice that does not qualify, for example a paid invoice in **Issue selected**, is skipped, and **Results** lists it with the reason.

## Export to CSV

Select **Export CSV**. The file holds every invoice that matches the current tab, search and filters, not only the rows on screen. Its columns are always in English:

`Type, Number, Status, Source, Client, Opportunity, Issue date, Due date, Currency, Subtotal, GST, Total, Paid, Credited, Amount due, Overdue`

Dates are written as YYYY-MM-DD (Singapore time) and amounts as plain numbers with two decimals. When the subtotal or the GST of an uploaded invoice is not known, the cell is empty, not 0.

At most 5,000 rows can be exported at once. When more match, Operon says so; narrow the filters and export again.
